{"schema":1,"function":"gumbel_ppf","description":"Gumbel distribution quantile function mu - beta log(-log p)","inputs":["mu","beta","p"],"outputs":["y"],"points":204,"tolerance":{"rel":1e-13,"reason":"p is an exact double. A careful method forms L = log(-log p) to a few ulps relative, also near p = 1/e where -log p is close to 1 (for example L = log1p(-log1p(d)) with d = e p - 1 formed in double-double); then mu - beta L costs (|mu| + |beta L|) / |mu - beta L| ulps, at most about 14 on this grid (mu = -10, beta = 1/4, p = 1 - 1e-15), 1.6e-15. 1e-13 as for the other quantiles"},"grid":"(mu, beta) in {(0, 1), (0, 2^-500), (0, 2^500), (-10, 1/4), (100, 8), (-2^1023, 2^1023)} x the gamma_ppf probabilities (p = 0, 5e-324, 1e-300, 1e-100, 1e-50, 1e-20, 1e-10, 1e-5, 1e-3, 0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.4, 1/2 - 1e-10, 1/2, 1/2 + 1e-10, 0.6, 0.75, 0.9, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999, 1 - 1e-5, 1 - 1e-10, 1 - 1e-15 and 1) and the doubles nearest 1/e and 1/e +- 10^-k for k = 5, 10, 15, where the quantile is near 0 for mu = 0; p = 0 and 1 are tagged pole (-inf and +inf), quantiles beyond the largest double are tagged overflow","mpmath":{"version":"1.4.1","dps":[50,100]},"scipy":{"version":"1.18.1","function":"scipy.stats.gumbel_r.ppf"},"numpy":"2.5.4","python":"3.13"}
